        "sole-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "What's the difference between Open Sole and Closed Sole?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Open Sole:</strong> heel open, mid-foot vent, true barefoot feel.</p><p><strong>Closed Sole:</strong> full coverage under the foot, heel included.</p><p>Same grip on both. The only difference is how they feel. Toes stay fully exposed either way. Both are $74.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/compare-open-closed-sole\">Open vs Closed: full comparison</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "sole-2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "Which style is better for reformer?",
            "answer": "<p>Either. Both soles perform identically on the Reformer, Cadillac Reformer, and Megaformer, and across Lagree, barre, and mat Pilates: same grip, same stability. Pick by feel: open heel and true barefoot feel (Open) or heel included (Closed).</p>"
          }
        },
        "grip-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "Do they really not slip?",
            "answer": "<p>Full contact 360\u00b0 grip across the underfoot, not silicone dots like a grip sock. It runs right to the edges, so you stay locked in through holds, transitions, and balance work.</p><p>No sliding. No resets.</p>"
          }
        },
        "studio-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "What workouts are they designed for?",
            "answer": "<p>Pilates and barre: reformer, Cadillac reformer, Megaformer, Lagree, Classical Pilates, barre, and mat. One 360° grip system across all of it. Some people also love them for TRX and yoga on and off the mat, and many wear them to hot Pilates and hot yoga with a thin sock if they sweat a lot.</p><p>Also great for weight lifting, outdoor volleyball, martial arts, barefoot running, outdoor yoga, and resortwear. Anywhere you'd go barefoot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "studio-2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "Will they make my feet hot or sweaty?",
            "answer": "<p>The opposite, in most cases. Toes stay fully exposed and the material is lightweight, so air circulates and they stay cooler than grip socks that wrap the whole foot. Open Sole adds an open heel and a mid-foot vent.</p><p>For hot yoga specifically, a thin full sock works like a towel. It absorbs the extra sweat without affecting grip.</p>"
          }
        },
        "surface-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "What surfaces do they work on?",
            "answer": "<p>All standard studio surfaces: reformer carriages, Megaformer platforms, wood floors, rubber mats, and yoga mats. Outdoors they hold on grass and pavement.</p><p>Wet tile, wet stone, and other slick floors are inherently slippery for any footwear. Always check the surface before you trust it.</p>"
          }
        },
