          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "Can I wear them barefoot or with a sock?",
            "answer": "<p>Both. They're designed for bare feet, and many people love that direct connection to the surface. Many others wear a thin sock underneath to cover their toes, stay warm, or soak up sweat in a hot class. Your practice, your call.</p>"
          }
        },
        "materials-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "What are Performance Skins made of?",
            "answer": "<p>A proprietary grip material. <strong>Skin safe. No latex. No silicone.</strong> Made in the USA.</p><p>The surface is non-porous, so sweat sits on it rather than soaking in the way it does with fabric.</p>"
          }
        },
        "price-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Product",
            "question": "Why $74 when grip socks are $20?",
            "answer": "<p>Because you buy them once. Grip socks run $18-28 a pair and lose their grip after six to eight washes, so most people go through 8-12 pairs a year: $144 to $336, every year.</p><p>Barreletics is $74 once. The grip is built into the sole, so it doesn't wash out. Buy 2 or more and save 10% with code SAVE2, applied at checkout. Shop Pay splits a pair into 4 interest-free payments of $18.50.</p>"
          }
